From 113e8fc83bf205f5e068d2b784a0ec8638967be8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:33:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] broadband-modem-qmi: add b2q-imsd backend for voice and
 messaging

Connect ModemManager Voice and Messaging interfaces to b2q-imsd
over D-Bus when the modem port has ID_MM_B2Q_IMS set. This enables
plasma-dialer and spacebar to work natively without requiring
QMI VOICE or WMS services.

Mobile-terminated SMS arrive as raw TPDUs (PduReceived, with the id of
b2q-imsd's durable inbox entry) and are acknowledged with AckPdu once
the part is handed to the messaging interface. Entries stored while
ModemManager was not running are fetched with GetPendingPdus when the
org.b2q.Imsd name appears.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L5scTPdTNcEmdyRhJMbUHU
